---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const MANIFEST = '/releases';
const DOCS = 'https://docs.freesense.org';
---

<Base
  title="Download FreeSense"
  description="Download manifest-driven FreeSense installer images for amd64 and verify their provenance and SHA-256 checksums."
>
  <section class="download-hero">
    <div class="wrap hero-grid">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Download center</span>
        <h1>Your firewall starts<br /><span>with a verifiable build.</span></h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Choose the supported Stable line or an experimental Development build, verify one
          checksum, and install or import on standard amd64 hardware. Every published image is tied to exact
          source, ports, OS-definition, and FreeBSD revisions.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#release-channels">View available images</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={`${DOCS}/getting-started/installation/`}>Installation guide</a>
        </div>
        <div class="platform-row" aria-label="Supported platform">
          <span>amd64</span><span>UEFI + BIOS</span><span>Signed repositories</span><span>Apache-2.0</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="release-terminal" aria-label="FreeSense release model">
        <div class="terminal-head"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>release contract</span></div>
        <div class="terminal-body mono">
          <p><b>$</b> resolve build-set</p>
          <p><em>source</em><span>exact commit</span></p>
          <p><em>ports</em><span>exact commit</span></p>
          <p><em>os-definition</em><span>exact commit</span></p>
          <p><em>freebsd</em><span>frozen snapshot</span></p>
          <div class="terminal-rule"></div>
          <p class="terminal-ok">verified artifacts only</p>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="release-channels" class="release-section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">Guided download</span>
          <h2>Choose the image that fits.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>Start with Stable for production. Cloud users can then choose UFS or ZFS and the disk format their platform expects.</p>
      </div>
      <div id="download-picker" class="download-picker-shell" aria-live="polite">
        <div class="loading"><span></span>Reading the release manifest...</div>
      </div>
      <p class="manifest-note">
        This picker stores no release versions. It reads independently published{' '}
        <a href={`${MANIFEST}/stable.json`}>Stable</a>{' '}and{' '}
        <a href={`${MANIFEST}/devel.json`}>Development</a>{' '}documents live from the package service;
        installer and cloud-image links point to immutable files on the download service.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pipeline-section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-heading compact">
        <div><span class="eyebrow">Independent build flow</span><h2>Rebuild only what changed.</h2></div>
        <p>System updates and optional packages have separate fingerprints, repositories, and publication decisions.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pipeline-grid">
        <article><span>01</span><h3>Check the System</h3><p>A daily planner builds and publishes the System repository only when its sealed inputs change.</p></article>
        <article><span>02</span><h3>Reuse optional packages</h3><p>Optional packages are reused while their sources and the pinned FreeBSD platform are unchanged. A System-only change does not rebuild them.</p></article>
        <article><span>03</span><h3>Publish after verification</h3><p>The ISO and every UFS/ZFS cloud image must pass integrity and boot-smoke checks. All immutable files are public before the channel document advances.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="architecture-section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">What is inside</span>
      <h2>A smaller, sharper platform.</h2>
      <div class="architecture-grid">
        <article><strong>32</strong><h3>Curated packages</h3><p>Each package declares capabilities, services, support state, and resource impact before installation.</p></article>
        <article><strong>8</strong><h3>Suricata generation</h3><p>Validated atomic configuration, EVE event browsing, service controls, and a focused security overview.</p></article>
        <article><strong>2</strong><h3>Modern network additions</h3><p>First-class CrowdSec response and consent-driven ZeroTier networking, integrated into the WebUI.</p></article>
        <article><strong>1</strong><h3>Sealed build set</h3><p>Every stage consumes the same resolved commits. Channel metadata points to exact verified artifacts; publication never rebuilds them.</p></article>
      </div>
      <a class="text-link" href={`${DOCS}/packages/installing-packages/`}>Explore the package platform <span aria-hidden="true">-&gt;</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="install-section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-heading compact">
        <div><span class="eyebrow">Installation</span><h2>From image to gateway.</h2></div>
        <p>Use a dedicated appliance or VM with at least two interfaces, or one VLAN-capable interface.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="install-steps">
        <li><span>01</span><div><h3>Verify the download</h3><p>Compare the ISO with the published SHA-256 checksum.</p><code>sha256sum FreeSense-*.iso</code></div></li>
        <li><span>02</span><div><h3>Write the installer</h3><p>Flash the ISO directly to a 4 GB or larger USB device with Rufus, Etcher, or dd.</p><code>dd if=FreeSense-*.iso of=/dev/DEVICE bs=4M conv=fsync</code></div></li>
        <li><span>03</span><div><h3>Boot and configure</h3><p>Assign WAN and LAN, open the WebUI, then replace the initial administrator password.</p><a href={`${DOCS}/getting-started/first-boot/`}>First-boot guide</a></div></li>
      </ol>
      <div class="requirements"><b>Recommended starting point</b><span>64-bit CPU</span><span>4 GB RAM</span><span>16 GB storage</span><span>2 network interfaces</span></div>
      <p class="cloud-warning"><strong>Cloud networking:</strong> Use two NICs so management remains on LAN. A one-NIC image permits key-only WAN SSH only when metadata supplies a valid key; restrict it with a cloud security group. The WebUI is never opened on WAN automatically.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<script define:vars={{ MANIFEST, DOCS }}>
  const channelMeta = {
    stable: { label: 'Stable' },
    devel: { label: 'Development' },
  };

  const escapeHtml = (value) => String(value ?? '')
    .replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/>/g, '&gt;').replace(/"/g, '&quot;');
  const size = (bytes) => {
    const value = Number(bytes);
    if (!Number.isFinite(value) || value <= 0) return '';
    if (value >= 1024 ** 3) return `${(value / 1024 ** 3).toFixed(2)} GiB`;
    return `${Math.round(value / 1024 ** 2)} MiB`;
  };
  const shortSha = (value) => value ? String(value).slice(0, 12) : 'not recorded';
  const releaseDate = (value) => {
    if (!value) return '';
    const date = new Date(value);
    if (Number.isNaN(date.getTime())) return '';
    return `${new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en', {
      dateStyle: 'medium',
      timeStyle: 'short',
      timeZone: 'UTC',
    }).format(date)} UTC`;
  };
  const changeTypes = {
    security: 'Security',
    fix: 'Fix',
    feature: 'Feature',
    ui: 'Interface',
    package: 'Package',
    documentation: 'Docs',
    build: 'Build',
    other: 'Change',
  };

  function provenanceBlock(release) {
    const p = release.provenance;
    if (!p || typeof p !== 'object') return '';
    return `<details class="channel-details"><summary>Build provenance</summary><dl>
      <div><dt>Source</dt><dd>${escapeHtml(shortSha(p.source))}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Ports</dt><dd>${escapeHtml(shortSha(p.ports))}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>OS definition</dt><dd>${escapeHtml(shortSha(p.os_definition))}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>FreeBSD</dt><dd>${escapeHtml(shortSha(p.freebsd))}</dd></div>
    </dl></details>`;
  }

  function changesBlock(release) {
    const changes = Array.isArray(release.changes) ? release.changes.slice(0, 20) : [];
    if (!changes.length) {
      return `<details class="channel-details changes empty">
        <summary><span>What changed</span><small>Not published</small></summary>
        <p>Release notes are not available for this build yet.</p>
      </details>`;
    }
    const rows = changes.map((change) => {
      const type = Object.hasOwn(changeTypes, change.type) ? change.type : 'other';
      const scope = change.scope ? `<span>${escapeHtml(change.scope)}</span>` : '';
      return `<li><i class="change-type ${type}">${changeTypes[type]}</i><div>
        <strong>${escapeHtml(change.title)}</strong>${scope}
      </div></li>`;
    }).join('');
    return `<details class="channel-details changes">
      <summary><span>What changed</span><small>${changes.length} ${changes.length === 1 ? 'change' : 'changes'}</small></summary>
      <ol>${rows}</ol>
    </details>`;
  }

  const artifactTypes = {
    installer: {
      label: 'Installer',
      title: 'Installer ISO',
      description: 'Bootable installation media for dedicated hardware and virtual machines.',
    },
    ufs: {
      label: 'UFS cloud',
      title: 'UFS cloud image',
      description: 'The recommended cloud image: compact, straightforward, and ready for root-disk growth.',
    },
    zfs: {
      label: 'ZFS cloud',
      title: 'ZFS cloud image',
      description: 'A larger cloud image with ZFS datasets and boot-environment support.',
    },
  };
  const artifactFormats = {
    iso: { label: 'ISO image', action: 'Download ISO' },
    qcow2: { label: 'QCOW2 (recommended)', action: 'Download QCOW2' },
    raw: { label: 'Raw GPT', action: 'Download raw GPT' },
  };
  const typeOrder = ['installer', 'ufs', 'zfs'];
  const formatOrder = ['iso', 'qcow2', 'raw'];

  function artifactsForRelease(release) {
    if (release?.schema_version === 'freesense.download/v2' && Array.isArray(release.artifacts)) {
      return release.artifacts.filter((artifact) => artifact?.url && artifact?.format);
    }
    if (!release?.url) return [];
    return [{
      kind: 'installer',
      format: 'iso',
      file: release.iso,
      url: release.url,
      size: release.size,
      sha256: release.sha256,
    }];
  }

  function artifactType(artifact) {
    if (artifact?.kind === 'installer' || artifact?.format === 'iso') return 'installer';
    return Object.hasOwn(artifactTypes, artifact?.filesystem) ? artifact.filesystem : '';
  }

  function artifactLabel(artifact) {
    const type = artifactTypes[artifactType(artifact)]?.title || 'Download image';
    const format = artifactFormats[artifact?.format]?.label || artifact?.format;
    return artifact?.format === 'iso' ? type : `${type} — ${format}`;
  }

  function checksumBlock(artifacts) {
    return `<details class="channel-details checksum"><summary>SHA-256 checksums</summary>
      ${artifacts.map((artifact) => `<p><b>${escapeHtml(artifactLabel(artifact))}</b><code>${escapeHtml(artifact.sha256)}</code></p>`).join('')}
    </details>`;
  }

  function noticeBlock(key) {
    return key === 'devel'
      ? '<div class="channel-notice experimental"><strong>Experimental &mdash; no support</strong><span>For labs and testing, never production.</span></div>'
      : '<div class="channel-notice supported"><strong>Recommended for production</strong><span>Immutable and supported throughout the 1.0.x line.</span></div>';
  }

  function pickerMarkup() {
    return `<div class="download-picker">
      <div class="picker-head">
        <div><span class="picker-kicker">Build your download</span>
          <h3>One clear path to the right image.</h3>
          <p>Choose a release, deployment type, and file format. The matching verified artifact appears below.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="platform-lock"><span>Platform</span><strong>amd64</strong><small>x86-64 &middot; UEFI + BIOS</small></div>
      </div>
      <div class="picker-controls" aria-label="Download options">
        <label class="picker-field"><span><b>1</b> Release</span>
          <select id="release-select" aria-label="Release"></select>
          <small>Stable is recommended.</small>
        </label>
        <label class="picker-field"><span><b>2</b> Image type</span>
          <select id="image-select" aria-label="Image type"></select>
          <small>Installer or cloud filesystem.</small>
        </label>
        <label class="picker-field"><span><b>3</b> Format</span>
          <select id="format-select" aria-label="Image format"></select>
          <small>Use QCOW2 unless raw is required.</small>
        </label>
      </div>
      <div id="picker-notice" class="picker-notice"></div>
      <div id="picker-result" class="picker-result" aria-live="polite"></div>
      <div id="picker-details" class="picker-details"></div>
    </div>`;
  }

  function mountPicker(target, channels) {
    const available = ['stable', 'devel'].filter((key) => {
      const release = channels[key];
      return artifactsForRelease(release).length > 0
        && (key !== 'stable' || release.support_tier === 'supported');
    });
    if (available.length === 0) {
      target.innerHTML = '<div class="not-available">No published release artifacts are currently available.</div>';
      return;
    }

    target.innerHTML = pickerMarkup();
    const releaseSelect = document.getElementById('release-select');
    const imageSelect = document.getElementById('image-select');
    const formatSelect = document.getElementById('format-select');
    const notice = document.getElementById('picker-notice');
    const result = document.getElementById('picker-result');
    const details = document.getElementById('picker-details');
    const requested = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);
    const requestedChannel = requested.get('channel');
    const requestedType = requested.get('image');
    const requestedFormat = requested.get('format');

    const replaceOptions = (select, options, preferred) => {
      select.replaceChildren(...options.map(({ value, label }) => {
        const option = document.createElement('option');
        option.value = value;
        option.textContent = label;
        return option;
      }));
      select.value = options.some((option) => option.value === preferred)
        ? preferred
        : options[0].value;
      select.disabled = options.length === 1;
    };

    const matchingChannel = available.find((key) => artifactsForRelease(channels[key]).some((artifact) => (
      artifactType(artifact) === requestedType
        && (!requestedFormat || artifact.format === requestedFormat)
    )));
    const initialChannel = available.includes(requestedChannel)
      ? requestedChannel
      : matchingChannel || available[0];

    replaceOptions(releaseSelect, available.map((key) => {
      const release = channels[key];
      const generation = key === 'devel' && Number.isInteger(release.generation)
        ? ` (g${release.generation})` : '';
      return {
        value: key,
        label: `${channelMeta[key].label} ${release.version || ''}${generation}`,
      };
    }), initialChannel);

    const selectedRelease = () => channels[releaseSelect.value];
    const selectedArtifacts = () => artifactsForRelease(selectedRelease());

    const render = () => {
      const key = releaseSelect.value;
      const release = selectedRelease();
      const artifacts = selectedArtifacts();
      const artifact = artifacts.find((item) => artifactType(item) === imageSelect.value
        && item.format === formatSelect.value);
      if (!artifact) {
        result.innerHTML = '<div class="not-available">This artifact combination is not published.</div>';
        return;
      }

      const type = artifactTypes[imageSelect.value];
      const format = artifactFormats[artifact.format];
      const version = release.version ? `FreeSense ${release.version}` : 'Current build';
      const generation = key === 'devel' && Number.isInteger(release.generation)
        ? `Generation ${release.generation}` : 'Stable release';
      const published = releaseDate(release.published_at || release.date);
      const file = artifact.file || String(artifact.url).split('/').pop();
      const guide = imageSelect.value === 'installer'
        ? { path: '/getting-started/installation/', label: 'Installation guidance' }
        : { path: '/getting-started/cloud-images/', label: 'Cloud deployment guidance' };
      notice.innerHTML = noticeBlock(key);
      result.innerHTML = `<div class="result-copy">
        <span class="picker-kicker">Selected download</span>
        <div class="result-title"><h3>${escapeHtml(type.title)}</h3><span>${escapeHtml(size(artifact.size))}</span></div>
        <p>${escapeHtml(type.description)}</p>
        <div class="result-tags"><span>${escapeHtml(version)}</span><span>${escapeHtml(generation)}</span><span>amd64</span>${published ? `<span>${escapeHtml(published)}</span>` : ''}</div>
        <dl class="artifact-facts"><div><dt>File</dt><dd>${escapeHtml(file)}</dd></div>
          <div><dt>SHA-256</dt><dd>${escapeHtml(artifact.sha256 || 'not recorded')}</dd></div></dl>
      </div>
      <div class="result-action">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="${escapeHtml(artifact.url)}">${escapeHtml(format.action)}<small>${escapeHtml(size(artifact.size))}</small></a>
        <a href="${DOCS}${guide.path}">${guide.label} <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
      </div>`;
      details.innerHTML = `<div class="release-details">${changesBlock(release)}${provenanceBlock(release)}${checksumBlock(artifacts)}</div>`;
      const url = new URL(window.location.href);
      url.searchParams.set('channel', releaseSelect.value);
      url.searchParams.set('image', imageSelect.value);
      url.searchParams.set('format', formatSelect.value);
      window.history.replaceState(null, '', url);
    };

    const refreshFormats = (preferred) => {
      const formats = formatOrder.filter((format) => selectedArtifacts().some((artifact) => (
        artifactType(artifact) === imageSelect.value && artifact.format === format
      )));
      replaceOptions(formatSelect, formats.map((format) => ({
        value: format,
        label: artifactFormats[format]?.label || format,
      })), preferred);
      render();
    };

    const refreshTypes = (preferred, preferredFormat = formatSelect.value) => {
      const types = typeOrder.filter((type) => selectedArtifacts().some((artifact) => artifactType(artifact) === type));
      replaceOptions(imageSelect, types.map((type) => ({
        value: type,
        label: artifactTypes[type].label,
      })), preferred);
      refreshFormats(preferredFormat);
    };

    releaseSelect.addEventListener('change', () => refreshTypes(imageSelect.value));
    imageSelect.addEventListener('change', () => refreshFormats(formatSelect.value));
    formatSelect.addEventListener('change', render);
    refreshTypes(requestedType || 'installer', requestedFormat || 'iso');
  }

  async function loadChannels() {
    const target = document.getElementById('download-picker');
    const channels = Object.fromEntries(await Promise.all(['stable', 'devel'].map(async (key) => {
      try {
        const response = await fetch(`${MANIFEST}/${key}.json`, { cache: 'no-store' });
        if (response.status === 404) return [key, null];
        if (!response.ok) throw new Error('release document unavailable');
        const release = await response.json();
        if (!['freesense.download/v1', 'freesense.download/v2'].includes(release.schema_version)
            || release.channel !== key) {
          throw new Error('release document invalid');
        }
        return [key, release];
      } catch {
        return [key, null];
      }
    })));
    mountPicker(target, channels);
  }
  loadChannels();
</script>

<style>
  .download-hero { position: relative; padding: 112px 0 84px; overflow: hidden; }
  .hero-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.35fr) minmax(320px, .65fr); gap: 72px; align-items: center; }
  h1 { margin: 16px 0 0; font-size: clamp(44px, 6vw, 74px); letter-spacing: -.055em; }
  h1 span { color: var(--coral-hi); }
  .lede { max-width: 720px; color: var(--muted); font-size: clamp(17px, 2vw, 21px); margin: 24px 0 0; }
  .hero-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; margin-top: 34px; }
  .platform-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; margin-top: 32px; }
  .platform-row span { padding: 5px 10px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 7px; color: var(--muted); font: 12px var(--mono); background: rgba(13,17,23,.55); }
  .release-terminal { border: 1px solid var(--border-2); border-radius: 18px; background: rgba(13,17,23,.86); box-shadow: 0 35px 90px rgba(0,0,0,.35); overflow: hidden; transform: rotate(1deg); }
  .terminal-head { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 7px; padding: 13px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); background: var(--ink-2); }
  .terminal-head i { width: 9px; height: 9px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--border-2); }
  .terminal-head i:first-child { background: var(--coral); }
  .terminal-head span { margin-left: auto; color: var(--muted-2); font: 11px var(--mono); }
  .terminal-body { padding: 24px; font-size: 13px; }
  .terminal-body p { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 20px; margin: 9px 0; }
  .terminal-body b { color: var(--coral-hi); }
  .terminal-body em { color: var(--muted); font-style: normal; }
  .terminal-body span { color: #d2d9e3; }
  .terminal-rule { height: 1px; background: var(--border); margin: 18px 0; }
  .terminal-body .terminal-ok { color: var(--good); justify-content: flex-start; }
  .terminal-ok::before { content: 'OK'; border: 1px solid rgba(62,207,142,.35); padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 5px; }

  .release-section { background: rgba(19,25,34,.82); border-block: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .section-heading { display: flex; align-items: end; justify-content: space-between; gap: 48px; margin-bottom: 38px; }
  .section-heading h2, .architecture-section h2 { margin: 10px 0 0; font-size: clamp(30px, 4vw, 46px); }
  .section-heading > p { max-width: 470px; color: var(--muted); margin: 0; }
  .download-picker-shell { min-height: 270px; }
  .loading { grid-column: 1/-1; display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; gap: 12px; min-height: 270px; color: var(--muted); }
  .loading span { width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--coral); box-shadow: 0 0 0 8px var(--coral-soft); animation: pulse 1.4s infinite; }
  @keyframes pulse { 50% { opacity: .45; transform: scale(.8); } }
  :global(.download-picker) { overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid var(--border-2); border-radius: 18px; background: linear-gradient(145deg, var(--ink-3), rgba(13,17,23,.9)); box-shadow: inset 0 1px rgba(255,255,255,.04), 0 22px 60px rgba(0,0,0,.2); }
  :global(.picker-head) { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 28px; padding: 28px 30px; }
  :global(.picker-head h3) { margin: 6px 0 8px; font-size: clamp(22px, 3vw, 30px); }
  :global(.picker-head p) { max-width: 680px; margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; }
  :global(.picker-kicker) { color: var(--coral-hi); font: 600 11px var(--mono); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .08em; }
  :global(.platform-lock) { flex: 0 0 auto; display: grid; min-width: 180px; padding: 14px 16px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 11px; background: rgba(13,17,23,.6); }
  :global(.platform-lock span) { color: var(--muted-2); font: 10px var(--mono); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .08em; }
  :global(.platform-lock strong) { margin-top: 3px; font: 600 18px var(--mono); }
  :global(.platform-lock small) { color: var(--muted); font-size: 11px; }
  :global(.picker-controls) { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0,1fr)); gap: 1px; padding: 1px 0; border-block: 1px solid var(--border); background: var(--border); }
  :global(.picker-field) { display: grid; gap: 8px; padding: 22px 24px; background: rgba(13,17,23,.82); }
  :global(.picker-field > span) { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; color: var(--text); font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; }
  :global(.picker-field > span b) { display: inline-grid; place-items: center; width: 20px; height: 20px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--coral-soft); color: var(--coral-hi); font: 600 10px var(--mono); }
  :global(.picker-field select) { width: 100%; min-height: 48px; padding: 0 13px; border: 1px solid var(--border-2); border-radius: 9px; outline: none; background: var(--ink-2); color: var(--text); color-scheme: dark; font: 600 14px var(--sans); }
  :global(.picker-field select:focus) { border-color: var(--coral); box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px var(--coral-soft); }
  :global(.picker-field select:disabled) { color: var(--muted); opacity: .8; cursor: not-allowed; }
  :global(.picker-field > small) { color: var(--muted-2); font-size: 11px; }
  :global(.picker-notice) { margin: 20px 30px 0; }
